    "source_assessment": "a359c6b1d73c and series head c33eb63d65a3 define Ac16/Xc16/Yc16 without GeneratePressureSet, and both generate the same 14-set tables. Downstream vendor/llvm-mos (pin 8be0546128a5, patch 0002) defines the same classes the same way. No local or upstream change sets GeneratePressureSet for MOS.",
    "binary_assessment": "The rebuilt a359c6b1d73c llc (sha256 2422c068...) is bit-identical to the split agent's deleted 321-01 llc, and its default hash table matches the split's 321-01/default-hashes.tsv. The rebuilt unchanged c33eb63d65a3 llc matches the split's 321-16 llc (b8006489...). Downstream build/llvm-mos MOSGenRegisterInfoTargetDesc.inc (d5c3510d...) has the same 14-entry tables. Its default-mode byte effect is unmeasured: no downstream build without the classes exists.",
    "decision": "New canonical record. mos-carry-scheduling-pressure concerns isPressureFineGrained not reaching the initial pressure sets, so carry pressure is lost. This record concerns opt-in classes adding pressure sets that change default-mode heuristics. The mechanism, the affected mode and the repair differ.",
