  "t4_design": {
    "description": "Keep GeneratePressureSet = 0 on Ac16/Xc16/Yc16 (generated tables = upstream) and, under +mos-a16 only, append pressure sets A16/X16/Y16 (limit 2) through MOSRegisterInfo overrides of the six pressure-set hooks; the sets are charged by each wide register's byte units and by Ac/Ac16, Xc/Xc16, Yc/Yc16; the native class also charges its low byte's generated sets.",
    "diff": {
      "path": "docs/defects/evidence/2026-09-30-native-width-pressure-sets/t4-design/change/change-321-01.diff",
      "sha256": "7b07b4c231dba7a8ff17dcee3f07a148114b1c5cad230031cf2bcb9af2880734"
    },
    "diff_at_head": {
      "path": "docs/defects/evidence/2026-09-30-native-width-pressure-sets/t4-design/change/change-321-16.diff",
      "sha256": "61e7e0444dfab32c2fcf585bdf633b1176e8cf2a3092ac16aceb4935744f8e61"
    },
    "native_at_head_vs_321_16": "+mos-a16 321489 -> 321411 B (-78; 16 larger, 4 smaller); +mos-a16,+mos-xy16 300012 -> 299850 B (-162; 15 larger, 5 smaller)",
    "cause": "With the flag alone the native classes have no pressure sets, so 16-bit vregs cost nothing to MachineLICM, MachineSink and the machine scheduler (all three contribute; all three disabled gives identical output). Restoring native-class pressure removes the native growth."
  }
}
